# Written and removed within one test by scripts/test-file-enumeration.test.ts
# (#1190): a copy of packages/db's vitest config with a different isolation list,
# which has to sit beside the real one because a project's include glob resolves
# against the config's own directory. Ignored so that a crashed run leaves a
# stray file rather than a dirty tree.
packages/db/vitest.*-probe.config.ts

# Generated on every build by packages/db/scripts/generate-storage-barrel.mjs.
# It is not in git on purpose (#271): a barrel with one line per storage module
# is an append point two agents collide in, and a file nobody commits cannot be
# merged at all.
packages/db/src/storage/index.ts

# An agent's own scratch worktrees. Claude Code puts a checkout of this
# repository under .claude/worktrees/, which git otherwise offers to add as an
# embedded repository and every tree walk descends into as a second copy of
# every source file. .prettierignore, eslint.config.js and
# scripts/test-file-enumeration.test.ts skip it for the same reason.
.claude/

# Produced by `scripts/build-changelog.mjs` from `packages/core/changes/`, and
# **not tracked** (`#1572`). A produced file that every entry touches is a file
# every pair of open pull requests conflicts on — 432 commits to it in thirty
# days — and `merge=union` resolves that in a working tree and is not applied by
# GitHub, so the conflict survived where it decides whether a branch can land.
# `#271` had already answered this shape: a file nobody commits cannot be merged
# at all. `changes/` is the changelog; `prepack` builds this for a publish.
packages/core/CHANGELOG.md

# Produced by `scripts/build-decisions-index.mjs` from `docs/decisions/`, and
# **not tracked either** (`#1662`, D-138). The same defect as the changelog above,
# reached the same way and cured the same way: two branches each adding a record
# regenerate this index, `merge=union` keeps both rows in a working tree, and
# GitHub never applies the driver — so the pair conflicts in the merge queue,
# where it reads as `UNMERGEABLE` and the entry is dropped quietly.
#
# `#1497` kept it tracked for a reader that was measured on 2026-08-24 and is not
# there: **no file in this repository links into `docs/decisions.md` by anchor.**
# `docs/decisions/` is the records; `npm run build:decisions` writes this for
# anybody who wants the one-page list.
docs/decisions.md
